  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TIEN SHAN BIODIVERSITY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed activity would be part of the Tien Shan Biodiversity Project (P104642), a regional project including Kazakhstan and Kyrgyz Republic. The objective of this activity would be to increase the pace and effectiveness of reforestation and afforestation activities in the Kyrgyz Republic. Increased reforestation would contribute to biodiversity protection, soil conservation, and carbon sequestration. IFAD will provide a $3 million grant so to ensure the necesary investment funding. During preparation, the team will also look for additional co-financiers. The activity would also contribute to develop a carbon trading scheme. The Bio-Carbon Fund would buy a share of the carbon credits generated.</narrative>
  </description>
